I was playing around in wizard mode when I noticed that
some teleportation items seemed to work on no-teleport
levels, namely Sokoban and the Castle. I'm used to being
able to teleport on those levels in wizard mode using the
control-T command, but I didn't know that scrolls of
teleportation worked there too.

I also noticed that when I tried to teleport into the Castle,
using a cursed spellbook and a ring of telecontrol (probably
redundant since wizmode gives you automatic telecontrol),
I got the "sorry..." message and was teleported somewhere
random outside the castle. I could, however, do a controlled
teleport to outside the castle.

I'd have thought that the obvious explanation was that
wizmoding takes away the no-teleport flags, but I'm not
sure why it'd still be impossible to teleport into the Castle
itself. Do any source-divers know exactly what's up here?
Would it be possible to reproduce any of these effects
outside of wizard mode? (Unfortunately I don't routinely
get far enough that I'd want to try these in a real game.)

Also, is there any circumstance under which a cursed
spellbook will teleport you and a scroll of teleport won't?
When I started off with this it seemed as though the cursed
book was teleporting me when I wouldn't expect to be
able to, but now it seems as though the scroll is working
in wizmode as well.


